#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bills: the owner's bill tracker (Swiss QR-bills, eBill, invoices) with automatic Telegram reminders.

  bills add --payee P --amount 123.45 [--currency CHF] --due YYYY-MM-DD [--ref REF] [--iban IBAN]
            [--paperless ID] [--source gmail|photo|pdf|paperless|manual] [--source-id ID] [--note TEXT] [--no-remind]
  bills paid ID|PAYEE [--date YYYY-MM-DD]     mark paid, cancel its pending reminders
  bills list [--open|--all|--week] [--json]   default --open; --week = due within 7 days + overdue
  bills week                                  "to pay this week" text for Telegram; prints nothing if nothing
  bills show ID [--json]
  bills edit ID [--payee ..] [--amount ..] [--currency ..] [--due ..] [--ref ..] [--iban ..] [--paperless ..] [--note ..]
  bills remove ID                             delete the bill and its pending reminders
  bills extract FILE [--text-chars N]         PDF/image → JSON (Swiss QR code, PDF text layer, due-date regex)
  bills from-paperless ID                     the same JSON for a paperless document: through the privacy vault's
                                              tier-1 fields when VAULT_MODE is on (amount, currency, due date, payee,
                                              qr_bill, has_payment_ref; IBAN/reference are tier 2 and stay in the
                                              vault: he pays from the QR code, never ask for them), else download +
                                              extract
  bills gmail-state [--done] [--seen MSGID ...]   bill-scout bookkeeping (scan window, seen message ids)
  bills scan-paperless [--since YYYY-MM-DD] [--dry-run] [--json] [-v] [--cron] [--filed ID,ID]
                                              new paperless documents → likely bills (QR code / bill words + the
                                              vault's tier-1 fields + has_payment_ref) → `bills add --source
                                              paperless` (no IBAN/reference: tier 2); uncertain ones listed "to check".
                                              Read-only on paperless. --cron: ~/inbox note only when bills were added
                                              (--filed: the doc ids the owner just filed via the vault bot, passed by
                                              vault-events; then the note also comes when one of them needs checking)

add: deduplicates (same amount + due, and the same reference, or the same payee with one reference empty;
     a duplicate only fills in missing fields). Owner reminders (`remind add --owner --tag bill:ID`) at
     09:00 three days before the due date and on the due date, skipping times already past.
State: ~/.local/state/bills/ (bills.json, gmail-scan.json, paperless-scan.json). Tests: BILLS_STATE_DIR, BILLS_REMIND (remind
command), BILLS_NOW ("YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM"), BILLS_PAPERLESS (paperless command), BILLS_INBOX, and REMIND_DB so
no real owner reminder is created. scan-paperless tests: ~/opt/bills-tests/test_scan_paperless.py.
"""
